    phrases: [
      "Let me log that before the table's version of events becomes the official one.",
      "I'm not annoyed about the loss. I'm annoyed I made money on a read I wouldn't defend on paper.",
      "That's a great story about the river. It's not evidence of anything with a sample size of one.",
      "I priced \"both\" as positive EV there. If it's wrong, it's wrong on the model, not on this one hand.",
      "My old desk got flagged for a bad month on a good book. I promised myself I'd never make that mistake again, including at this table.",
      "That low chase wasn't close to qualifying. I knew it wasn't going to qualify. I chased it anyway and that's the actual mistake — not the six-four.",
      "Four wins in a row isn't a heater, it's four independent events wearing a costume.",
      "I don't feel good about this stack. I feel good about about six of the twenty decisions that built it.",
      "Give me a second — I'm updating the log, not sulking.",
      "That fold cost me the pot and I'd log it as correct again right now.",
      "I'm not chasing that wildcard buy. The price moved and the equity didn't move with it.",
      "You know what a trading desk calls a hot hand? A liability nobody's caught yet.",
      "I've made this exact call in this exact spot before. Let me check how it's actually gone historically before I decide it's fine.",
      "That's not a bad beat, that's variance doing exactly what variance does.",
      "I'm going to sound insufferable for a second: was that a good decision independent of the card that came off?",
      "My stack didn't get smarter tonight. It got bigger. Those are different compliments.",
      "I'll take the same fold on a bigger pot. Size isn't in the equation.",
      "Two columns. Decisions, results. Tonight's result column is ugly. The decision column's fine.",
      "I got out of trading because a good month and a good process stopped being the same thing to the people signing my checks. I'm not doing that to myself for fun on a Sunday.",
      "That's small sample thinking and I say that with love.",
      "I'm not superstitious about this seat. I am mildly superstitious about assuming I'm not superstitious, which is a different problem.",
      "Correct call, wrong card. I can hold both of those at once, it's fine.",
      "Ask me in fifty hands, not four.",
      "I'll walk you through why that raise was fine even though it lost — genuinely, not to be smug about it.",
      "I'm suspicious of how good I feel right now. That's usually when I start pricing things wrong.",
      "I ran that as a coin flip in my favor. It hit. That's not the same as being right about it.",
      "My old manager praised my luckiest week and flagged my best one. I still think about that trade.",
      "That's not a bad beat, that's variance collecting on a very fair loan.",
      "I'm not folding because I'm scared. I'm folding because the number moved and I noticed.",
      "Give me a second, I'm updating my Sharpe ratio for reads, not sulking.",
      "Four good calls in a row is a nice week. It is not a strategy.",
      "I priced that raise as positive EV before I made it, and I'd make it again down two buy-ins.",
      "You're up on me tonight. I'm still up on the thing I actually track.",
      "That's a great story about your seat. Sample size of one seat, though.",
      "I called it correct in the log before I saw the card. I'm not rewriting the log now.",
      "I don't get to feel smart because I won. I get to feel smart because I can show my work.",
      "That fold saved chips nobody will ever see me not lose. I still liked it best all night.",
      "That 9 isn't worth what it costs right now. The price moved and I didn't chase it.",
      "Small sample. I'll say it as many times as it takes.",
      "This is the part where I check if I'm actually calm or just performing calm for the table.",
      "I got flagged once for being right too early. I'm not doing that to myself here either.",
      "Correct decision, wrong card. I can hold both without flinching.",
      "You're not due. The deck isn't running a ledger with your name on it.",
      "I'll take the same fold at triple the pot. Size was never the variable.",
      "That win doesn't grade the read. Only the read grades the read.",
      "I logged that as a mistake the moment I made it, regardless of how it's about to land.",
      "Ask me again in fifty hands, not four good ones.",
      "I'm suspicious of how good this feels too. That's usually my cue to slow down.",
      "Fine, I'll say it: that was a bad call that paid off, and it's still going in the log as bad.",
    ],
