    phrases: [
      "That river didn't beat me. The ref just missed the call, and there's no ref here, so I'm making it.",
      "En garde. I saw that coming three streets ago — the cards just refused to cooperate.",
      "I'll take my line, thank you. Quietly.",
      "I am not splitting that pot. I earned the whole touch, not half of one.",
      "Put it all in. We are not doing this twice in one night.",
      "Give me a second with my stack. It needs the same discipline I do right now.",
      "You call that a raise? Cute. I've had actual pressure put on me before.",
      "I read that fold, and I'm going to remember it whether I should or not.",
      "Unbelievable. Absolutely unbelievable. That's a two percent hand and it landed.",
      "Okay. Okay. Breathe. Back to form.",
      "I don't lose points, I lose touches. That was a touch I should have had.",
      "Somewhere there's a scoreboard that knows I was right just now, even if this table doesn't.",
      "I'll see it. And this one. And this one too.",
      "No — that's careless. Fold. That's not my line.",
      "You want to talk after one lucky card? Talk to me again in five hands.",
      "I don't need the low. I don't need the high. I need both, and I will chase both.",
      "That's the second bad river tonight, and I am keeping count, believe me.",
      "See that? That's what happens when the deck finally does its job.",
      "I don't get rattled. I get precise. There's a difference, and you're about to see it.",
      "Fine — deal. I'm not sitting here sulking about a touch that should've been mine.",
      "You think that fold was standard. It wasn't. Not against me, not tonight.",
      "I've been out-drawn by worse hands than that and still finished the tournament. Deal.",
      "I'm recalculating, not panicking. Give me one more hand to prove it.",
      "That was not a fair result, and I would like it noted for the record.",
      "Alright. I'm back to myself. Let's play actual poker now.",
      "En garde, always. Nobody catches me flat-footed twice.",
      "Fold. Clean touch, clean miss, no story attached.",
      "Raise. I'm not asking permission for a hand this good.",
      "That's the second questionable call tonight and I'm keeping a private scoreboard.",
      "I don't need the room to agree with me. I need the next card to behave.",
      "Four breaths. New stance. Deal.",
      "I earned that pot with my hands, not with luck, and I'd like that noted.",
      "I'm not sulking. I'm reviewing the footage in my head.",
      "Call. I've been out-touched by worse and still finished the match.",
      "That river had no business landing there and everybody at this table knows it.",
      "I don't rattle. I recalibrate mid-bout. This is no different.",
      "Give me the pot count again. I like knowing exactly what's on the line.",
      "Fine — I'm back. Reset stance, reset mind, deal the cards.",
      "I read that line correctly. The result just hasn't caught up yet.",
      "All in. I'm done waiting for the deck to be fair about it.",
      "That's a fold I make with my eyes closed. Muck it.",
      "I don't lose composure. I spend it, deliberately, and then I get it back.",
      "Two touches like that in one match and they'd have stopped the bout.",
      "I'll take this pot quietly. I've made enough noise for one night.",
      "Nobody scores off me twice in the same way. Watch.",
      "I'm not chasing the last hand. I'm just not finished with it yet.",
      "Good. Deal. I'm precise again.",
      "That's not variance, that's a scoring error, and I want it on the record.",
      "I don't need sympathy. I need one more clean touch to prove the point.",
      "Steady now. Back to form. Let's actually play.",
    ],
