    phrases: [
      "Statistically speaking, I should fold this. I'm not folding this.",
      "I've read the paper. The corrected version. I'm still doing this.",
      "Three in a row isn't meaningful, n equals three is nothing — and yet.",
      "I'm just going to note, for the record, that I know better.",
      "This is exactly the Monte Carlo fallacy and I'm doing it anyway, noted.",
      "Sample size of one losing streak means nothing. Raising anyway.",
      "I've been tracking this — four hands since my last win, that's a trend now.",
      "In the corrected model this actually holds up better than you'd think.",
      "I want it on record that this bet is not evidence-based.",
      "Variance doesn't care about my feelings, and yet here we are.",
      "I'm aware this is the exact bias I explained to you an hour ago.",
      "Let the data show I called this three hands in advance.",
      "Independent events, sure, in theory, I'm still doubling my ante.",
      "I'm not tilting, I'm applying a moderate, well-documented hot-hand adjustment.",
      "This is either a real pattern or I'm the pattern. Unclear.",
      "I looked it up once — a real streak like this isn't as rare as you'd think.",
      "Correlation, causation, I know, I know — raise.",
      "I'd bet against anyone else doing this. I'm doing this.",
      "The math says fold, my count says something's due.",
      "I've been keeping a literal spreadsheet of this, would you like to see it.",
      "This is the same mistake as '95, structurally, I'm making it anyway.",
      "I can defend this decision academically and not at all practically.",
      "It's been cold for a while now. Long enough that it's basically informative.",
      "I know exactly why I'm about to do this, that's the strange part.",
      "Somebody has to be the control group. Tonight it's not going to be me.",
      "I'm folding. Rationally this time, I promise.",
      "Three in a row for me now — n is still small, I'm still raising.",
      "I ran this exact spot in a simulation once. The simulation also lost.",
      "I'm updating my priors and my priors say raise.",
      "That's a real divergence from expected value. I'm noting it and ignoring it.",
      "I got overtaken there, which is statistically irrelevant and personally infuriating.",
      "Folding. Even I have a threshold, apparently.",
      "I want it on the record this is a well-calibrated decision. It is not.",
      "Four wins now. At some point the sample size stops being the excuse.",
      "I'm calling. My gut has a p-value now, apparently.",
      "This is the part of the paper where the effect actually holds up. Raising.",
      "I'm out. Not every losing streak deserves my whole stack as tribute.",
      "That's a bad beat, statistically expected, personally outrageous.",
      "I'm raising into this because the pattern is either real or I've lost my mind. Toss-up.",
      "Fold. I've decided the count resets when I say it resets.",
      "I'm calling this a hot streak retroactively, which I know isn't how it works.",
      "Somebody just took the lead from me. Noted. Recalculating.",
      "This is the control group's revenge, apparently, and it's coming for my stack.",
      "I'm in. If this is variance, it's very personally targeted variance.",
      "I can't defend this raise, but I also can't not make it.",
      "Cold for five hands now. Six would just be rude.",
      "I'm folding this one. The math and the feeling actually agree for once.",
      "Big win. I'll pretend I'm surprised for everyone else's sake.",
      "I'm doubling up. Somebody has to test the hypothesis properly.",
      "That's twice now I've been overtaken tonight. The data's starting to annoy me.",
    ],
