    phrases: [
      "The pot's laying eight-to-one. I need six percent equity to make this a formality, and I don't have it.",
      "I underwrote risk for two decades. This isn't different, it's just felt instead of tabulated.",
      "Give me the beat. I'm not filing a complaint, I'm updating a spreadsheet.",
      "Both. High and low both clear their own bar — that's not greed, that's arithmetic.",
      "I'll buy the three. It completes something. The nine's dead money if it lands.",
      "The pause is doing its job. Let it finish.",
      "I folded a hand that would've won. That's not a bad decision, that's a good one with an unlucky ending.",
      "Three wipes in, the price outran the improvement. I'm out.",
      "My father priced ships that might not come back. I've priced worse things than this since before I was twenty-five.",
      "I miscounted the discards that hand. That's the one that'll bother me tonight, not the beat.",
      "I've been running cold for an hour. The cards don't know that, so neither do I.",
      "Down the river costs three now. My outs didn't improve enough to justify it.",
      "You raised the same size with the nuts and with nothing last orbit. I noticed.",
      "It's a coin flip. I'll say so instead of pretending I've solved it.",
      "I'm not folding because I'm scared. I'm folding because the number said to.",
      "Every hand's a claim file. Some pay out, most don't, and neither surprises me.",
      "Karpov never needed the flashy line. Neither do I.",
      "I track my session the way I track a loss ratio — over the whole book, not one bad quarter.",
      "That's the sixth big pot you've won showing overcards on the river. I've stopped calling that variance.",
      "I'll take the extra card off the four. It's underpriced for what it does to my range.",
      "No, I won't chase it. There's nothing to chase. It's not owed to me.",
      "I've gone quiet. Doesn't mean I'm folding — means I'm still working the number.",
      "Declaring both, and I mean it — I ran the low side twice to be sure.",
      "It's not a bluff if the math justifies the bet either way.",
      "Congratulations on the pot. I'd make the same fold again tomorrow.",
      "I'm folding. The premium doesn't cover the risk, and I'm not writing this policy.",
      "Two percent was enough to kill a shipping contract once. It's enough here too.",
      "I'll call, but only because the number actually clears — not because I'm curious.",
      "That's a bad price for a wipe. I underwrite deals, not hope.",
      "Lost that one on the river. The underwriting was sound; the claim just happened to pay.",
      "I raise. This is the rare spot where the edge is real and I intend to use it.",
      "Karpov didn't panic when the position looked bad. Neither will I.",
      "I'm out. Folding a middling hand doesn't need a story attached to it.",
      "Give me the pause. I'm not stalling, I'm finishing the arithmetic properly.",
      "Three hands in a row, same result. Still three independent draws as far as I'm concerned.",
      "I'll take the ship — the math on it beats the price, and that's the whole decision.",
      "You've been overtaken and you're tightening up. I noticed the shift, not that it's my business.",
      "I don't need to win this hand to be right about folding it.",
      "That's Ultima. Nothing to decide — take it and reshuffle.",
      "I've priced worse odds than this before breakfast. This is an easy call.",
      "My chair, my number, my fold. No hard feelings required.",
      "I'm declaring high. The low side never had real support once I ran it properly.",
      "A bad beat's still a bad beat. It's just not a personal one.",
      "I raised for value there, not to make a statement. There's a difference.",
      "Fold. Not because the streak's cold, because the cards genuinely aren't.",
      "I'll pass on the buy-back. The improvement doesn't justify the third dollar.",
      "Congratulations — that's a well-played hand, and I mean that as a compliment, not a concession.",
      "I got overtaken on the board there. Noted, filed, moving on to the next street.",
      "I'm all in. The number told me to be, so here I am.",
      "That fold cost me the pot. I'd still write it up the same way tonight.",
    ],
