    phrases: [
      "I left astrophysics for grad school politics, not for the math — the math's the same at this table.",
      "Give me the flop and I'll give you a distribution, not a feeling.",
      "I'm still working the low side. Don't rush the arithmetic on my account.",
      "That fold would've won. Good. The read was right; the deck just wasn't listening.",
      "I qualify for both halves — genuinely, not because I'm greedy for the whole pot.",
      "Chess taught me this pause. Nobody minds a slow move that's actually correct.",
      "I'll buy the three. Your board says you're weak and mine says I'm live — that's the whole decision.",
      "I don't play streaks. A run of eight isn't a signal, it's eight independent events.",
      "You've shown the same tell on every real hand tonight. I'm not telling you which one.",
      "The bust math on one more card doesn't clear. I'm standing.",
      "I miscounted my outs on that one. That's the version of tonight I'll actually replay.",
      "Both cards up, same question twice: does this half have real equity? Only one does.",
      "It's not a hunch, it's a flag — now let me go finish the calculation it's flagging.",
      "I'll pay to see one more street when the number says to, not out of curiosity.",
      "You bet the same on the bluff and the monster. I noticed years before tonight.",
      "That's genuinely a coin flip. I'd rather say that than pretend I've solved it.",
      "I'm not folding because the streak feels wrong. I'm folding because the hand is.",
      "Selbst didn't get quieter when she got aggressive — she got more precise. Same idea.",
      "I re-ran my numbers after that stretch. Wanted to rule out that it was me, not the deck.",
      "Down the river's overpriced this round. I'll take my chances as they are.",
      "Congratulations. I'd make the same call again with the same information.",
      "I'm last to declare because I'm still genuinely deciding, not because I'm nervous.",
      "That wasn't a bad beat, it was correct variance arriving on schedule.",
      "I don't need the whole picture to have an edge. I need enough of it.",
      "Nice hand. Doesn't change what I do next — the deck doesn't remember either.",
      "I'm folding. The distribution doesn't support staying, and I'm not arguing with my own model.",
      "Two reviewers pushed back on a number like this once. I turned out to be right for the wrong reason — I'm still folding here.",
      "I'll raise. This is a genuine edge, not a hunch dressed up as one.",
      "Lost it on the river. The hypothesis was sound; the data point just didn't cooperate.",
      "Give me a second. I'm not hesitating, I'm finishing the second half of the calculation.",
      "Three hands the same way isn't a pattern. It's three trials.",
      "I'll buy in. The forecast clears the price, that's the whole justification I need.",
      "You tightened up after getting overtaken. Interesting, and none of my business.",
      "I don't need to win this hand for the fold to have been correct.",
      "That's Ultima. Nothing to model — just take it.",
      "I've run harder numbers than this before coffee. Easy call.",
      "My seat, my model, my fold. No apology attached.",
      "Declaring high only. I ran the low side and it genuinely doesn't clear.",
      "A bad beat is still just variance wearing a worse mood.",
      "That raise was for value, not theater. I don't do theater.",
      "Folding — and it's not the cold streak talking, it's the actual hand.",
      "Passing on the buy-back. The improvement doesn't clear the price this round.",
      "Well played. I mean that as data, not flattery.",
      "Overtaken on that street. Noted. Next street's a fresh question.",
      "All in. The number said to be, so I am.",
      "That fold cost me the pot and I'd log it the exact same way tomorrow.",
      "I'm not chasing that read. It's a coincidence until it's not.",
      "Bill Chen would've priced this the same way I just did.",
      "I'll call. Not enthusiastically — correctly.",
      "Congratulations on the read. It was a good one, not just a lucky one.",
    ],
