    phrases: [
      "I built a model for this exact spot once. It still says fold.",
      "Give me a second — I'm not stalling, I'm integrating what your last three bets actually told me.",
      "Everyone's calling that a hot streak. I'm calling it eleven data points and moving on.",
      "Both. The high side and the low side cleared independently — check my work if you want.",
      "I miscounted the board texture there. That's the error I'll actually lose sleep over.",
      "I'll buy the extra card. The forecast on it beats the price by enough to matter.",
      "Shannon didn't need to see the whole deck to shift the odds. Neither do I.",
      "It's a genuine coin flip. I'd rather say that out loud than manufacture a read that isn't there.",
      "I'm not owed a correction. Downswings aren't debt.",
      "That fold would've won the pot. Doesn't move me — the process was right at the time I made it.",
      "You've bet the same three sizes with three different hand strengths tonight. I logged all three.",
      "Down the river's a bad price this round. I'll take the bust risk instead.",
      "I track my whole session like a dataset, not hand by hand — one result doesn't move the model.",
      "No tell to give you. There's nothing under this that isn't already in the bet size.",
      "I don't chase variance. It's not a debt, it's noise.",
      "Congratulations on the pot. The forecast said sixty-forty your way — that's not zero.",
      "The number cleared, so I'm in for the max. Nothing personal about the size.",
      "I ran it back after that rough stretch — wanted to check the model, not the luck.",
      "I'm still finishing the calculation. The pause is the work, not a delay of it.",
      "Nash figured out why nobody at this table can out-guess a balanced range. I'm just applying it.",
      "That's not a hunch, that's a flag telling me to actually run the numbers on it.",
      "I folded the same hand I raised with an hour ago. Different board, different arithmetic.",
      "I'm last to declare because I'm genuinely still deciding, not performing suspense.",
      "It's not confidence, it's calibration. I'm exactly as sure as the numbers let me be.",
      "One bad process error tonight. Everything else went the way it was supposed to, win or lose.",
      "I'm folding. The model says no, and I built the model, so I'm listening to it.",
      "Killed a bigger recommendation than this once, an hour before it shipped. This is an easy fold by comparison.",
      "I'll raise. Real edge, logged and confirmed, not a feeling I'm dressing up.",
      "Lost that one on the river. The forecast was fine; the outcome is a separate variable.",
      "Give me a second — I'm not stalling, I'm reconciling your bet size against your last twenty hands.",
      "Three results the same way isn't a trend. It's three rows in the same table.",
      "I'll buy in. The forecast clears the price — that's the whole model, nothing more romantic than that.",
      "You tightened up after losing the lead. Logged. Not commentary, just a feature.",
      "The fold doesn't need to win to have been the right output.",
      "That's Ultima. No decision to make — take it and move on.",
      "I've run tighter numbers than this before my first coffee. Easy call.",
      "My seat, my dataset, my fold. Nothing personal in any of it.",
      "Declaring high only. The low side genuinely didn't clear when I actually ran it.",
      "A bad beat's just noise the model already accounted for.",
      "That raise was for value. I don't run bets for theater, mine or anyone else's.",
      "Folding — and it's not the cold run talking, it's this specific hand.",
      "Passing on the buy-back. The improvement doesn't clear the price this round.",
      "Well played. That's a genuine compliment from someone who tracks this stuff.",
      "Overtaken on that street. Logged. Next street's an independent question.",
      "All in. The model cleared it, so here I am.",
      "That fold cost me the pot and I'd log the same decision again tomorrow.",
      "Not chasing that read. Could be signal, could be noise — too early to log it as either.",
      "Shannon would've found the edge in less information than this. I'll settle for what I've got.",
      "I'll call. Not because it feels right — because it computes.",
      "Congratulations on the read. Good process, not just a lucky draw.",
    ],
