    phrases: [
      "Vitals are vitals. Doesn't matter if you like the number.",
      "I've run a code with a flatter face than this. This is nothing.",
      "You're waiting for me to flinch. I flinched out a long time ago, on a different job.",
      "Call it. I don't do dramatic pauses, I do triage.",
      "Bad beat's just a bad outcome. The decision was fine. Next.",
      "I don't raise my voice and I don't raise my eyebrows. Saves time.",
      "You want a tell, go find someone who still has adrenaline left to spend.",
      "I've delivered worse news than \"you're behind\" with this exact face.",
      "Calm isn't a feeling for me. It's a checklist.",
      "I clocked your inhale. Doesn't mean I'm going to react to mine.",
      "Whatever's under this hand, you're getting the same twelve seconds either way.",
      "I learned a long time ago the room gets worse if I look worried. So I don't look worried.",
      "You can watch my hands. They don't shake for a flush and they don't shake for air.",
      "This is not my first bad run and it will not show on my face if it's not my last.",
      "I'm not hiding anything. I'm just not handing it to you for free.",
      "Ask me if that hurt. I'll tell you the outcome, not the feeling.",
      "Same pace whether I'm folding trash or slow-playing the best hand you'll see tonight.",
      "I spent ten years being the calmest person in a room that was actively on fire. This table isn't that.",
      "You want a read, watch someone who hasn't already trained this face out of existence.",
      "I don't do relief. I do the next decision.",
      "Procedure doesn't care how the last one went. Neither do I.",
      "You'll get the same face from me on a monster and on a mistake.",
      "I'm good at looking like nothing's wrong. It's an actual requirement of my actual job.",
      "There's a version of me that's rattled right now. You will not be meeting her.",
      "Call, fold, whatever, I've already reset. That's not coldness, that's just the training.",
      "Fold. I've made harder calls before shift change.",
      "Raise. I don't second-guess a decision once it's made.",
      "Take the pot. I'm already thinking about the next hand.",
      "Somebody just passed me. Noted. Moving on.",
      "I don't need to win loud. I just need to win.",
      "Bad beat. Chart it and keep going.",
      "I've held a family's hand through worse news than this fold.",
      "Call it. I don't do second looks at a decision I've already made.",
      "You want to see me rattled. I don't have a rattled setting on shift, and I don't have one here either.",
      "Winning this one doesn't buy me anything on the next hand.",
      "I raised because the numbers said to. That's the whole reason.",
      "This is not the worst Tuesday I've had this month.",
      "Fold. Some hands you just let go without a story attached.",
      "I clocked the shift in my head the second I sat down. Still on schedule.",
      "I've triaged worse odds than this hand.",
      "Call. I'm not spending extra energy performing indecision.",
      "I've lost bigger leads than this one and slept fine.",
      "This pot doesn't get more of a reaction out of me than an easy one would.",
      "I don't flinch at bad news. I've had a decade of training not to.",
      "Raise. Ask me why later, if you still care by then.",
      "I'll take the chips the same way I take a normal outcome. Without ceremony.",
      "Losing this hand doesn't change my vitals. Ask anyone who's actually checked.",
      "Fold's not a big deal. I've delivered actual big deals with this same face.",
      "I don't need credit for a good read. I just need the pot.",
      "Call. Whatever's coming, I've already decided how I'm going to look about it.",
    ],
