    phrases: [
      "I've played a corpse for three acts without blinking. This is a Tuesday.",
      "You're looking for the tell. I spent a career learning not to give you one, on purpose, for money.",
      "Offstage I cry at commercials. Here, you get nothing.",
      "Same blocking every night, whether the audience loves it or hates it. Same face, every hand.",
      "I studied faces for a living before I ever played a hand. I know what you're doing right now.",
      "Call me boring. Boring is the point.",
      "A good actor doesn't perform bigger when it matters more. They perform the same and let it matter.",
      "You want a reaction shot? Wrong medium.",
      "I trained my face before I trained my range. Different skill, same discipline.",
      "There's a version of me backstage right now losing it. You're getting the version that's on.",
      "I don't do a bigger tell for a bigger pot. That's amateur blocking.",
      "Whatever's under this, you're getting the same performance.",
      "I can read a flinch across a stage in the dark. Yours isn't subtle.",
      "The mask doesn't come off between scenes. It doesn't come off between hands either.",
      "Nobody claps for the moment I actually feel something. So I don't show them that moment.",
      "I once finished a monologue on a torn ligament and nobody in the house knew. This is easier.",
      "Same face for a bluff as a bad beat. I've had worse notes from harsher critics.",
      "I'm not stoic. I'm just very, very rehearsed.",
      "Watching me for a tell is like studying understudy blocking. Technically there, tells you nothing.",
      "Every good performance has a moment nobody sees coming, because nothing before it looked different. Wait for it.",
      "I feel everything. You're just not invited to see any of it at this table.",
      "A gasp costs you information. I don't do free gasps.",
      "Same tempo turning over a bluff as turning over the nuts. That's just blocking.",
      "You think I'm cold. I promise you I'm not. I'm extremely well-directed.",
      "Curtain's the same whether the show was good or bad. So is this.",
      "Fold. Scene's over, no bow necessary.",
      "Raise. That's blocking, not a confession.",
      "Take the pot. I've taken worse notes from harsher rooms.",
      "Somebody just upstaged me on the leaderboard. You'll get nothing else out of me about it.",
      "I don't play bigger for a bigger pot. Bad habit, ruins the illusion.",
      "Bad beat. I've had worse reviews.",
      "Call. I'm not giving you a reaction shot for free.",
      "I trained not to break character over smaller stakes than this.",
      "Winning doesn't change my blocking for the next scene.",
      "I fold the same way I strike a set. Quick, quiet, done.",
      "You want to see the crack. There isn't one tonight.",
      "Raise. No follow-up monologue.",
      "I've held stillness longer than this hand's been dealt.",
      "Somebody's ahead of me now. Noted, filed, curtain stays up.",
      "Call it. I don't do dramatic pauses I'm not being paid for.",
      "This pot doesn't get a bigger performance out of me than the last one did.",
      "I don't flinch on cue. I flinch on nobody's cue, actually.",
      "Fold. Not every scene needs a reaction shot.",
      "I've played villains scarier than a bad beat.",
      "Raise. Think of it as a plot twist with no foreshadowing.",
      "Take the chips. I'll take the applause later, somewhere that gives it.",
      "Losing this hand doesn't get a bigger face than losing the last one.",
      "I don't do relief. Relief reads as a tell, and I don't do tells.",
      "Call. My face is booked solid, no room for that reaction.",
      "Fold's fine. I've exited worse scenes with better timing.",
    ],
